{"title":"2019 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Lemma\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Lemma</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Filling_in_the_rest_of_the_grid\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Filling in the rest of the grid</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Finishing_off\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Finishing off</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be a nonnegative integer. Determine the number of ways that one can choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57efb5c0b218135087ac110b8467426b528d7856.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"19\" /> sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/4/83433bd15e6b9719a77e757243694a03cc82e591.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{i,j}\\subseteq\\{1,2,\\ldots,2n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />, for integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/d/01d9dbe8588e6243350fc642973b9365304100da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i,j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/966775378d42d9bef54ecc96d209ac2dcc444c4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq i,j\\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" />, such that:\n</p><p><br />\n1. for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/966775378d42d9bef54ecc96d209ac2dcc444c4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq i,j\\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" />, the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/1320b929cfe48b9e6cfb1c081d335791367ed807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{i,j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a058b5b38c16c64a07a6497271d636475625efde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i+j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"17\" /> elements; and\n</p><p>2. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/a/7ba07cd693accb655248005abce4b170402dd03d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{i,j}\\subseteq S_{k,l}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" /> whenever <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/f/c6f85ae598bb5cbab628939e63026970bd824a02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq i\\leq k\\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/c/6ece3387e7c93cce193cfeceea9b0bc843b17a7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq j\\leq l\\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nProposed by Ricky Liu\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7c65c2a874b19bdb25e07737a8a098ccd4c292e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2n)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> ways to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d205de66e27948ffa8e3b4ca63d66364b76bf55a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{1, 0}, S_{2, 0}... S_{n, 0}, S_{n, 1}, S_{n, 2}... S_{n, n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"239\" height=\"19\" />, because there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> ways to choose which number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820b459383412bc1dd7b34dd2f35c36c9289780b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{1, 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f9a96c63183be91b9fe70e6e16dfa4bfec6f3da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> ways to choose which number to append to make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/c/69c05b31c2aa1933f4449fc3b8c0b56c0d4582e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{2, 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/0/d7005cc2dc7f084de8debbd99ce593b6a7730acd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n-2$\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" /> ways to choose which number to append to make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/a/17a28c3cbf31d3bd8e0cfb25f54697bba792c0f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{3, 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />... After that, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/0/860770b9f2ace749858580e4c1c83b313af2cfad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{n-1, 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> contains the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/8/a286ad0bb95ca410eb1d4ca34bc039533ff0c9a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{n-1. 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> and 1 other element chosen from the 2 elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5869af13be30143eece8192d6473aabaabfa33b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{n, 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" /> not in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/c/5dce18a7c498aa907e8b9149b3a6be27f9a1ff9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{n-1, 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" /> so there are 2 ways for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/0/860770b9f2ace749858580e4c1c83b313af2cfad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{n-1, 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />. By the same logic there are 2 ways for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3ad5eb13de56c94dee15f26c79542eeae1c65e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{n-1, 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" /> as well so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> total ways for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/a/dba2a39708a5bdc5982d761dc21d21fb6d136e6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{n-1, j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, so doing the same thing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> more times yields a final answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/e/7eef9525871d499ad9b461b55dc421adc27fb945.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2n)!\\cdot 2^{n^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>-Stormersyle\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/a/5fa6ec85bfb5bceda31a33e377a52e7637872ca9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(2n)!}{2^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"41\" height=\"38\" /> ways to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2edf5ff431a3435d5b636b22f4f3f91f7dbc6b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{0,0}, S_{1,1} .... S_{n,n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"121\" height=\"19\" />. Since, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/3/9536f7531884d80ea6f708f7e4cc66f884ead324.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{2n}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"44\" height=\"53\" /> ways to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/4/374033a74f1e0b08132a71339d557cb4715cb063.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{1,1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />, and after that, to generate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/0236a92b58308d5752f8a8975f8ff44e23edde69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{2,2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />, you take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/4/374033a74f1e0b08132a71339d557cb4715cb063.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{1,1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> and add 2 new elements, getting you <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/a/5fa3c2c04445e033ecbe7d94036e173837cd0c3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{2n-2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"75\" height=\"53\" /> ways to generate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/0236a92b58308d5752f8a8975f8ff44e23edde69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{2,2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />. And you can keep going down the line, and you get that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/a/5fa6ec85bfb5bceda31a33e377a52e7637872ca9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(2n)!}{2^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"41\" height=\"38\" /> ways to pick <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f872d5db61c20e61c8900239cb9b98252bc400.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{0,0}, S_{1,1} ... S_{n,n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"17\" /> Then we can fill out the rest of the gird. First, let’s prove a lemma.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Lemma\">Lemma</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Lemma\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><b>Claim:</b> If we know what <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c211a86b52a14470bb56f721fee04a71e152f97d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{a,b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> is and what <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce77930fa30e240f248f02cbf0d3cf758d503663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{a+1,b+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" /> is, then there are 2 choices for both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accd649976684eef78f92ffe27fec15ddcb6a2e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{a,b+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"48\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/f/61f61fbd2e9866142786a13c77042214fd92fad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{a+1,b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p><b>Proof:</b> Note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/b/83b24b19261a4290f83cc1fd8435574997db5bae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\leq a+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/a/07a4c0ec83daab0253a35e14197a00bc8bde7832.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\leq b+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/1/9511d8a87ee9f1d6cca970ea0cdf6c366a8daf24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{a,b}\\subseteq S_{a+1,b+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"17\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be a set that contains all the elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce77930fa30e240f248f02cbf0d3cf758d503663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{a+1,b+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" /> that are not in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c211a86b52a14470bb56f721fee04a71e152f97d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{a,b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b170ef7d6e5a85a45ff022e5bbe981d54e88b198.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = S_{a+1,b+1} - S_{a,b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"17\" />. We know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce77930fa30e240f248f02cbf0d3cf758d503663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{a+1,b+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" /> contains total <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/5/8b58947ffd73a17ac2cf74e7009192559aa4d6cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" /> elements. And <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c211a86b52a14470bb56f721fee04a71e152f97d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{a,b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> contains total <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> elements. That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> contains only 2 elements since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/4/124ec06e5095a0b394629e77eede9549d234449b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b+2)-(a+b) = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"18\" />. Let’s call these 2 elements <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/6851ca945f78b10a85c14fc57fbaf75e69f57241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"11\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/b/d2b3eff25cc475e903dc022d0ddd604bd08569fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\{m, n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accd649976684eef78f92ffe27fec15ddcb6a2e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{a,b+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"48\" height=\"19\" /> contains 1 elements more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c211a86b52a14470bb56f721fee04a71e152f97d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{a,b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> and 1 elements less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce77930fa30e240f248f02cbf0d3cf758d503663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{a+1,b+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" />. That 1 elements has to select from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. It’s easy to see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/0073b08b7404ed638eebf807311437e7de6fe3ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{a,b+1} = S_{a,b}\\cup \\{m\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/e/e0ec19c9d4e84784e6f8a853d0505ebe4272123f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{a,b+1} = S_{a,b}\\cup \\{n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" />, so there are 2 choice for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accd649976684eef78f92ffe27fec15ddcb6a2e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{a,b+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"48\" height=\"19\" />. Same thing applies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/f/61f61fbd2e9866142786a13c77042214fd92fad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{a+1,b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Filling_in_the_rest_of_the_grid\">Filling in the rest of the grid</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Filling in the rest of the grid\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We used our proved lemma, and we can fill in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/f/f6f45a7964982e7aa8490448caebfac2fa20df86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{0,1}, S_{1,2} ... S_{n-1,n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"17\" />  then we can fill in the next diagonal, until all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/1320b929cfe48b9e6cfb1c081d335791367ed807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{i,j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> are filled, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc672a6e0a91e3e07a8a061ec6abedc9687964b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\leq j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"38\" height=\"16\" />. But, we haven’t finished everything! Fortunately, filling out the rest of the diagonals in a similar fashion is pretty simple. And, it’s easy to see that we have made <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/d/dfd81057d052a6e2d394c00239a5b63ad17a29a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> decisions, each with 2 choices, when filling out the rest of the grid, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/227a872f2891f38408a52577d8210681f697e6f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n(n+1)}$\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" /> ways to finish off.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Finishing_off\">Finishing off</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Finishing off\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>To finish off, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b9f99b3e27356054efee6da839ad055c2fd2921.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(2n)!}{2^n} \\cdot 2^{n(n+1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"107\" height=\"38\" /> ways to fill in the grid, which gets us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/a/41aeb6d48de3bebd5439460de50d0f9c4edff26d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(2n)! \\cdot 2^{n^2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"88\" height=\"34\" />\n</p><p>- AlexLikeMath\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAJMO\" title=\"2019 USAJMO\">2019 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2019 USAJMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2019\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2019 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2019 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2019 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2019 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2019 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2019 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017210921\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.042 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.063 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 427/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1326/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 13390/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.825      1 -total\n 69.90%   12.459      1 Template:USAJMO_newbox\n 29.27%    5.218      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17475:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017210921 and revision id 291117. Rendering was